GRADE U2: true — V2 HOLDS — THE FINDING. His `T4` conjunct, lifted byte-for-byte out of his instrument at `ff93ad0a` (true) and round-tripped after the one substitution that makes it drivable (true):

    const renamedAway = !/\btype Row\b/.test(readFileSync(join(REPO, PROBE_371_PATH), 'utf8').slice(readFileSync(join(REPO, PROBE_371_PATH), 'utf8').indexOf('ROUND 396 RE-KEY')));

`indexOf` refuses with **-1** and `.slice(-1)` is the last CHARACTER of the string. Measured rather than reasoned (331): with the marker gone the slice is **1** character(s) of a 25293-character file, and `/\btype Row\b/` cannot match one character — so the test is false and the conjunct is **true**. ONE AXIS, and the pair carries the IDENTICAL defect: both `KP` and `CF-1` reintroduce `type Row` immediately after the marker; the only thing that differs is whether the string `ROUND 396 RE-KEY` is still spelled that way. Anchors asserted unique before anything was substituted (true; 347).

| case | marker | defect after it | slice | his conjunct |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| CONTROL-A | true (indexOf 19518) | false | 5775 chars | **true** (as predicted) |
